        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: शिरः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शिरः (śiraḥ) — \"head\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शिरः (śiraḥ) is the head. The old family it belongs to gathered around a sense of \"head, horn\": Greek kara, \"head\", and Latin cerebrum, \"brain\", sit in it, and so — further out — does English horn."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit has a second head-word, mūrdhan, for the top or the summit of a thing. शिरः (śiraḥ) is the ordinary one: the head you nod, the head you bow when you say नमस्ते."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three of five, and the bow you already knew has a body part in it now."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
